  "conclusions": [
    "Nonempty overlap does not imply that separating valid actions is impossible or harmful.",
    "A too-large margin can conflict with narrow valid support even when supports are disjoint; this is not specific to shared prefixes.",
    "Multiple valid actions do not justify forcing identical vectors or averaging their modes."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Finite valid sets are stipulated for logic checks, not estimated from rollout data.",
    "No task success, learned-policy effect or novelty result is measured.",
